From: Airtel AAP321NK port
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_mpd: tolerate foreign bootinfo SMEM size

On a kernel-only boot (tftp/bootm of just the Linux FIT on top of the
vendor's already-running SBL+TZ firmware), SMEM item 507
(UPD_BOOT_INFO_SMEM_ID) may already be allocated by the vendor Q6/TZ stack
at a size different from the upstream-hardcoded 4096. SMEM is allocate-only
and lives in a reserved region untouched by bootm, so our kernel inherits
that foreign item and the original `size != 4096` check aborts Q6 bring-up
even though qcom_smem_get() returned a valid mapping.

The bootinfo payload actually written is tiny, so fail only on a real error
pointer and merely warn on a foreign size, then proceed -- letting the
handshake advance to the Q6/TZ firmware's own version/auth validation.

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
@@ -324,13 +324,20 @@
 	}
 
 	ptr = qcom_smem_get(REMOTE_PID, UPD_BOOT_INFO_SMEM_ID, &size);
-	if (IS_ERR(ptr) || size != UPD_BOOT_INFO_SMEM_SIZE) {
+	if (IS_ERR(ptr)) {
 		dev_err(wcss->dev,
 			"Unable to acquire smp2p item(%d) ret:%ld\n",
 			UPD_BOOT_INFO_SMEM_ID, PTR_ERR(ptr));
 		return PTR_ERR(ptr);
 	}
 
+	/* A foreign (vendor-allocated) item of a different size is tolerated on
+	 * kernel-only boots over vendor firmware; the payload written is tiny. */
+	if (size != UPD_BOOT_INFO_SMEM_SIZE)
+		dev_warn(wcss->dev,
+			 "bootinfo smem(%d) size %zu != %d, proceeding (vendor-allocated)\n",
+			 UPD_BOOT_INFO_SMEM_ID, size, UPD_BOOT_INFO_SMEM_SIZE);
+
 	/*Version*/
 	version = (wcss->desc->bootargs_version) ? wcss->desc->bootargs_version : VERSION2;
 	memcpy_toio(ptr, &version, sizeof(version));
